{"seconds": 44.5, "exit": 0, "final": "Black plays Kxe5 or Bxe5, and White has won the exchange (rook for bishop). This is clearly winning for White.\n\nNe5+ is the best move. The key tactical point is that after the forcing check, the Black rook on d8 is undefended, and White captures it. Black's best try (Kf6, Kh7, Kg7) all allow Rxd8, winning the exchange.\n\n**Best move:** Ne5+\n\n**Main line:** Ne5+ Kh7 Rxd8 Bxe5 (or Ne5+ Kf6 Rxd8 Kxe5, or Ne5+ Kg7 Rxd8 Bxe5)\n\n**Motif:** fork (the check forces the king to move, leaving the rook undefended)\n\n**Explanation:** After Ne5+, Black's rook on d8 is undefended and attacked by White's rook on d5. Any king move (Kh7, Kg7, or Kf6) leaves the rook hanging. White continues with Rxd8, winning the exchange (rook for bishop). The lesson: a forcing check can flush the king away and leave the opponent's pieces undefended.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Ne5+\", \"line\": [\"Ne5+\", \"Kh7\", \"Rxd8\", \"Bxe5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "3r4/3N4/6k1/P2R1ppp/8/6b1/6P1/5K2 w - - 11 43"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "3r4/3N4/6k1/P2R1ppp/8/6b1/6P1/5K2 w - - 11 43"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "3r4/3N4/6k1/P2R1ppp/8/6b1/6P1/5K2 w - - 11 43"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r4/3N4/6k1/P2R1ppp/8/6b1/6P1/5K2 w - - 11 43", "move": "Ne5+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r4/8/6k1/P2RNppp/8/6b1/6P1/5K2 b - - 12 43", "move": "Bxe5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r4/3N4/6k1/P2R1ppp/8/6b1/6P1/5K2 w - - 11 43", "move": "Nf8+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r1N2/8/6k1/P2R1ppp/8/6b1/6P1/5K2 b - - 12 43", "move": "Rxf8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "3r4/3N4/6k1/P2R1ppp/8/6b1/6P1/5K2 w - - 11 43", "move": "Rd6+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "3